1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
A support handoff needs the incident facts,
not every personal detail or instruction.

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:09,000
This is Handoff Gate.

3
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:15,000
Clocked Protect identifies sensitive spans.
The app validates their positions and transformation.

4
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:21,000
Only transformed text moves on
to the instruction check.

5
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:27,000
Guard treats the ticket as untrusted content,
checked against a fixed support scope.

6
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:33,000
A ticket cannot approve itself
or override the application permissions.

7
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:39,000
Inspect assesses the proposed script
without running it.

8
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:46,000
A benign ticket cannot overrule
a risky recovery command.

9
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:52,000
Export opens only when the transformation
and both risk results meet the local policy.

10
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:59,000
Share redacted facts and a decision summary,
not original contact values or script source.

11
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:05,000
Uncertain, malformed or failed results
require human review.

12
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:10,000
Authored replay is labelled separately.
It is never presented as a live result.

13
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:15,000
Three Clocked integrations.
English and Traditional Chinese views.

14
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:20,000
Fictional examples. No script execution.
Human responsibility.
